      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The claims about immediate bankruptcy are alarmist and lack rigorous, peer-reviewed data supporting a total collapse. While increased population certainly requires resource allocation, studies consistently show that the long-term economic contributions of immigrants—through taxes and labor participation—outweigh the initial costs. Those who fear budget strain often focus only on short-term, immediate expenditures without accounting for the sustained economic growth immigrants generate.",
      "source": "target",
